  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.485–0.650) dramatically outperform image-only models (0.208–0.227), and the best configuration so far is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc. The critical unresolved question is whether the image modality, despite its very weak standalone performance, provides any complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. This experiment tests that question in the most controlled way: it pairs the best-performing RNA setup (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool) with the simpler image encoder (resnet50) and simplest fusion (concat), changing only the addition of the image branch relative to config_005. If config_030 fails to beat 0.650, it strongly indicates that image features are uninformative for this task, allowing us to eliminate all 36 multimodal configurations and focus remaining budget on RNA-only refinements. If it does improve, it confirms complementary signal and justifies further exploration of fusion strategies and image encoders. This is the highest-information single experiment under the limited budget because it resolves the largest remaining design uncertainty (is multimodality worth pursuing at all?) with a minimal, interpretable change."
}

